      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think, the check implemented with this approach is not very meaningful. `asin` expects a value in the domain [-1, 1]. If the effect modifies the amplitude of the input sinusoid, the output from `asin` will not be correct. Also, `asin` can only return the value in the range [-pi/2, pi/2], thus \"folding\" input phases on that interval. As a result, the calculated difference might not be correct. Basically, the test only indicates whether there is any phase shift at all. For that, we could just compare `left[j] \u003d\u003d right[j]`, or compare whether input is the same as output directly. Thus, since the test just happen to detect presence of any alteration to the input signal, it can be radically simplified.",
